#!/bin/bash
# Crypto Screener V3 TRUTH loop — self-paced, read roadmap and execute first unchecked task
# Run: claude "/loop $(tail -1 CRYPTO_LOOP_V3.sh)"
# Or paste the last line into claude with /loop

Read docs/CRYPTO_SCREENER_V3_TRUTH_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task. Doctrine recap: NEVER serve or display per-coin data from a symbol-matched source without the price cross-check gate (source last price vs CG/base price within 3%, stables 1% — else nulls + blacklist); join by CG id not symbol wherever the source provides ids (CG categories/trending); honest '—' beats plausible numbers — missing numeric is null never 0, no fake +0.00%; llama TVL protocols only count when protocol.mcap agrees with CG mcap within 0.3x-3x, TVL under 1M USD is null. Standing constraints: NO new serverless files (all server work via ?view= branches in api/crypto/markets.ts), vercel.json keeps "regions":["fra1"] (Binance 451-blocks US), keyless APIs only and curl-verify each NEW endpoint from prod before coding against it, no new npm deps, additive payloads (v1/v2 fields + coingecko-coinlore-okx chain untouched), th/td parity for any ColKey change. Audit tooling: apps/market-ui/scripts/audit_crypto_coverage.mjs writes docs/CRYPTO_COVERAGE_AUDIT.md — rerun it to measure every task's effect and paste REAL coverage/mismatch numbers into the Progress log. Verify per task: market-ui typecheck 0 + vercel --prod + prod curl with real numbers. Flip the task to [x], append one Progress-log line, commit on roadmap/world-class (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). PERSISTENCE: never end the loop because of a usage/rate limit, 429, or overloaded error — on any such error stop consuming tokens, ScheduleWakeup at 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log + CRYPTO_COVERAGE_AUDIT.md are recovery state; log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations); chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining, or a task blocked on something only the user can provide — then say exactly what's needed and still ScheduleWakeup (3600s) so the loop resumes if supplied.
